     Server List Configuration

     Purpose:
       This file defines the servers that the application will connect to.

     Structure:
       <ServerGroup> contains multiple <Group> entries.
	   Each <Group> must include:
         - Code     : Unique numeric ID (0–19)
         - Name     : Max 32 characters
     
	 Example:
       <Server Code="0" Name="SSeMU Classic" />
	   <Server Code="1" Name="SSeMU Rebirth" />
		 
       <ServerList> contains multiple <Server> entries.
       Each <Server> must include:
         - Code     : Unique numeric ID (0+)
         - Name     : Max 32 characters
         - IP       : IPv4 address
         - Port     : Port number (1-65535)
         - Visible  : 0 (hidden) or 1 (visible)

     Example:
       <Server Code="0" Name="SSeMU Server 1" IP="192.168.1.10" Port="55900" Visible="1" />
       <Server Code="1" Name="SSeMU Server 2" IP="192.168.1.11" Port="55901" Visible="0" />
-->

<ServerGroup>
	<Server Code="0" Name="SSeMU Classic"/>
</ServerGroup>

<ServerList>
    <Server Code="0" Name="SSeMU Server 1" IP="LAN/WAN IP" Port="55900" Visible="1" />
</ServerList>